---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro'
import { site } from '../data/site'
import '../styles/pages/privacy.css'

// The privacy policy for Jarvis, Lucas's personal home dashboard. Google's OAuth consent screen links here.
const description = 'Privacy policy for Jarvis, the personal home dashboard Lucas Bianco built: what it reads from Google Calendar, how it is used, and how to remove access.'
---

<Base title="Privacy policy" description={description}>
  <PageHeader
    title="Privacy policy"
    crumbs={[{ href: '/', label: 'Home' }]}
    measure="Jarvis · last updated November 2026"
    lede="Jarvis is a personal dashboard I built for my own room. This page explains what it reads from Google and what happens to it."
  />

  <section class="section privacy-body">
    <div class="frame">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>Who this covers</h2>
        <p>
          Jarvis is a private, personal project. Its only user is me, Lucas Bianco. It is not a public app, it has no
          sign-ups, and it is not offered to anyone else.
        </p>

        <h2>What Jarvis reads from Google</h2>
        <p>Jarvis asks Google for two read-only permissions on my own Google account:</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>See my list of calendars</strong> (<code>calendar.calendarlist.readonly</code>).</li>
          <li><strong>See the events on those calendars</strong> (<code>calendar.events.readonly</code>).</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          It cannot create, change or delete events, and it asks for nothing else: no email, contacts, files or
          other Google data.
        </p>

        <h2>How it is used</h2>
        <p>
          The events are shown on screens in my room: today's timeline, upcoming deadlines and reminders. That is the
          only use.
        </p>

        <h2>Where it is stored</h2>
        <p>
          Event data is kept only on my own devices, a small computer at home that runs the dashboard. The sign-in token
          is stored in a private settings file on those same devices and never published.
        </p>

        <h2>Sharing</h2>
        <p>
          Google data is never sold, shared with anyone, sent to other companies, used for advertising, or used to
          train AI models. No analytics or tracking services receive it.
        </p>

        <h2>Limited Use</h2>
        <p>
          Jarvis's use and transfer of information received from Google APIs adheres to the
          <a href="https://developers.google.com/terms/api-services-user-data-policy">Google API Services User Data
          Policy</a>, including the Limited Use requirements.
        </p>

        <h2>Keeping and deleting data</h2>
        <p>
          Events are refreshed regularly and older copies are replaced. Access can be removed at any time from
          <a href="https://myaccount.google.com/permissions">Google Account → Third-party connections</a>; after that,
          Jarvis can no longer read anything, and I delete its stored copy from my devices.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions about this policy: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
